      "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nProvide an mRoPE tensor when capturing Transformer Engine CUDA graphs. When multi-latent attention is disabled, the graph helper includes rotary inputs for RoPE but omits mRoPE, so replay silently drops position embeddings and produces different losses and gradients from eager execution. The captured tensor provides the input shape; replay supplies the actual embeddings.\n\nThis affects graph training independently of activation offloading. In BF16 Qwen3.5-0.8B language-model training with local pretrained weights and tokenized training data at `aecc0e8116912554f27a62a51ad2aeca479a7f9e`, eager and graph states match before capture and diverge on the first replay with offloading disabled. Vision and MTP were not included.\n\n## Validation\n\n- At `5df3661919c5119830d089fb6f8aa0cc5e0d14d8`, which merges `main` at `581248531984920e92f076946ad4629d359442a4`, a native GPT/DDP test on one RTX PRO 6000 compares loss and all main gradients for two different three-axis positions and passes. The pre-fix implementation previously failed this regression with a loss mismatch.\n- On the earlier dependent commit `c5264b66197040f4309edfdb22dc9bbaf62189b1`, full BF16 Qwen3.5-0.8B language-model training matches eager and graph loss, gradients, weights and full optimizer states for six steps on one GPU and on both ranks with TP2+SP.\n- Black, isort, Ruff, Pylint and the kernel-determinism coverage checker passed on the changed files. Upstream GPU CI has not run.\n\n[Current-head commands, rank logs and checksums](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/Megatron-LM/tree/8b0e8560eb1c41713564b20152dec9aecf5001f6/gdn-conflict-20261030). [Earlier Qwen training evidence](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/Megatron-LM/tree/02890e97b1273d9a8695f76aaa208730054fe415/gdn-open-issues-20261027) is retained at its original revisions.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nRelated to #8308.\n\n## Code provenance\n\nNo code copied or adapted from external repositories.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n### Pre-checks\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests.\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests.\n- [x] The determinism coverage checker passes; no numerical kernel is changed.\n- [x] I have added proper typing to the changed code.\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation.\n- [ ] I have run the complete autoformatter script.\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
